  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Low pressure continues to withdraw and improving\nconditions expected overnight.  \n\nA vigorous upper-level trough continues to swing across the\nNortheast U.S. tonight and into Saturday. The main surface low \nis now well offshore and will continue to move away across the \nNorth Atlantic overnight. The widespread precipitation across \nthe region has been ending from SW to NE today and this trend \nwill continue into the evening. While the best dynamics will \nmove away, there will still be opportunities for extra \ncloudiness and scattered showers across the far NW areas. These\nwill develop as a result of upstream lake-effect activity across\nNorth PA and upstate NY. \n\nIt'll remain cold tonight with lows dropping below normal. Lows\nwill reach the upper 20s to low 30s in most areas. Winds will \ndecrease from 10 to 15 mph to 5 mph or so later tonight. \n\nKey Message 2...Below normal temperatures continue this weekend into \nearly next week. \n\nAs low pressure moves into the Canadian Maritimes this weekend and\nhigh pressure builds to our west, northwesterly flow will continue\nto usher in cold air into the region. This will keep temperatures\nslightly below normal through the weekend into early next week. In\nfact, a Freeze Warning is in effect tonight through Saturday morning\nfor all counties whose growing season has not ended with the exception\nof Philadelphia County which has a Frost Advisory. If the cold does\nnot end the growing season for any of these areas, another Freeze\nWarning/Frost Advisory is possible the next couple of days as\nwell.\n\nIn addition to the colder temperatures, winds will be gusty during \nthe day due to a tight pressure gradient across the area through the \nweekend with winds gusts of 20-30 mph possible.\n\nWith the cold air and northwest flow, there will also be the possibility\nfor some lake effect/lake enhanced snow or rain showers in the Poconos\nand higher elevations of Sussex County, New Jersey as well.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Widespread minor coastal flooding is expected to continue tonight \nfor portions of Ocean County New Jersey and Sussex County Delaware. \nFlooding will be confined mainly to back bay areas. \n\nWater levels have diminished for most areas following this morning's \nhigh tide. However levels remain elevated in back bay areas of Ocean \nCounty New Jersey and Sussex County Delaware where a Coastal Flood \nAdvisory is in effect until 4 AM Saturday. This includes Rehoboth \nBay and Little Assawoman Bay in Delaware and Barnegat Bay in \nNew Jersey. Some places may stay above minor flooding thresholds\nthrough this afternoon's low tide before waters levels come up \nagain with the high tide later this evening. Expect levels to \nremain below moderate thresholds so the Coastal Flood Warning \nfor Ocean County was converted to an Advisory. For the day \nSaturday and beyond, no further flooding is expected as NW winds\nshould help flush out water trapped in the back bays.",
